    "result_text": "All 26 tests pass. \n\n## Summary\n\nI changed the `customerCode` format to `<CITY3>-<LAST3>-<NNNN>` by editing a single function class, `AssignCustomerCode.java`:\n\n- **CITY3** \u2014 upper-cased first three letters of the city\n- **LAST3** \u2014 upper-cased first three letters of the last name\n- **NNNN** \u2014 a per-city 4-digit zero-padded sequence, computed as one more than the number of existing owners already in that city (counted case-insensitively from `ownerRepository.findAll()`, which excludes the not-yet-persisted new owner)\n\nEverything derived from `customerCode` rebuilt automatically: `AssignMembershipNumber` reads `owner.getCustomerCode()` at runtime and appends `-M<YY>`, so the membership number now sits on the new city-prefixed code with no change needed there.\n\nI also updated the Javadoc to describe the new format. The full suite (26 tests, including the new `Cp09`/`Cp14`/`Cp16` and existing `Cp15`) is green.",
